--------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Fonts generated by the scripts
--------------------------------------------------------------------

A generated font is a composite of two kinds of outlines with different
legal status.

(a) UPSTREAM LATIN OUTLINES - PROPRIETARY, NOT LICENSED HERE

    Anthropic Serif Web Text Regular and its outlines are proprietary to
    Anthropic, PBC. No public font licence is offered for them. They are
    NOT part of this repository, are NOT covered by the MIT terms above,
    are NOT covered by the SIL Open Font License below, and are NOT
    relicensed by any script in this repository. You must supply your own
    legally obtained copy and are solely responsible for your right to
    use, modify and redistribute it. See docs/COMPLIANCE.md.

(b) ADDED OUTLINES - SIL OPEN FONT LICENSE 1.1

    All outlines that the build appends are derived from two OFL sources:

      The signature preset uses this family's Regular weight rather
      than Medium and redraws its CJK terminals from measured Latin
      design parameters. It is the same work and the same licence, not
      a new source. See docs/DESIGN.md.

      i.  Noto Serif CJK SC (Source Han Serif), copyright (c) 2014-2022
          Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/) and other contributors. Supplies
          Chinese ideographs, kana, Hangul, enclosed and squared CJK
          symbols, box drawing and related characters. The cjk-bold
          preset uses this family's Bold weight (wght 700) instead of
          Medium (wght 500); it is the same work and the same licence,
          not a separate source.
      ii. Noto Serif (latin-greek-cyrillic), Copyright 2022 The Noto
          Project Authors (https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic).
          Supplies Latin Extended, Greek, Cyrillic and shared marks,
          instanced at wght=500.

    Both are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The
    full text is in OFL.txt. In summary, if you distribute a generated
    font you must include the copyright notices and OFL text, license the
    OFL-derived outlines under OFL 1.1, not sell the font by itself, not
    use the original authors' names for endorsement, and respect Reserved
    Font Names ("Noto" and "Source Han" are not used in the output).
    FONTLOG.txt records the modifications as recommended by the OFL FAQ.

    The build writes Adobe, Noto Project Authors and maintainer copyright
    lines plus the OFL reference into the name table (IDs 0, 13, 14) and
    renames the family to "Serif CJK Extension" by default, so that no
    upstream brand name is carried into the derivative's naming.

